# Global AI Rules for Library Management System

## Architecture Rules
- All code MUST follow a 3-layer architecture: Models → Services → Storage
- Services MUST depend on abstract repository interfaces, NOT concrete implementations (Dependency Inversion)
- NO external databases or APIs — all data is stored in-memory using Python collections
- All public classes and methods MUST have type hints and docstrings

## Design Pattern Rules
- Strategy pattern is used for fine calculation — do NOT hardcode fine logic in services
- Observer pattern is used for event-driven notifications — use EventManager for cross-service communication
- Repository pattern is used for data access — all storage operations go through repository interfaces

## Code Quality Rules
- Follow SOLID principles strictly
- No code without interfaces first — define ABCs before implementations
- TDD: Write tests before or alongside implementation
- All functions must have explicit return types
- Use dataclasses for domain models
- Use enums for status fields
- Custom exceptions must inherit from LibraryError

## Testing Rules
- Minimum 70% code coverage required
- Use pytest with pytest-cov for coverage
- Use pytest-mock for mocking dependencies
- Integration tests must test full workflows across multiple services
- Each test class should focus on a single unit (class or function)

## File Organization
- Models: src/models/
- Services: src/services/
- Storage: src/storage/
- Utilities & Patterns: src/utils/
- Tests: tests/unit/ and tests/integration/
